{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And may His enemies be from those who rise.</b> The verse's saying ״מִן יְקוּמוּן״ — according to our Sages of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 99:2) — prophesies concerning the kingdom of Greece, which is destined to fall by the hand of the Hasmoneans. Therefore he said ״וּמְשַׂנְאָיו מִן יְקוּמוּן״, meaning: even at the very time when the haters have an uprising and Israel are lowly, at that very time ״מְחַץ מָתְנַיִם קָמָיו״ etc., and so it was; and this matter is a success through miracle and wonder."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:08.734644686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}